  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 329 AM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nStrong west-northwest flow continues as we head into midweek, with \nat least some threat for thunderstorms continuing as well. This \nstrong flow aloft will keep ample deep layer shear in place on \nWednesday, and some threat for strong to severe storms appears \npossible. Confidence in both placement and coverage of storms \nremains low confidence for now, and trends will continue to be \nmonitored. By late week, upper ridging will begin to establish \nacross the Rockies, amplifying into the weekend. This upper \nridge axis also begins to translate eastwards into the Plains by\nSaturday night. This will lead to height rises across the area \nand increasing temperatures into the weekend. This could also \nbring a brief reprieve from thunderstorm threats, before the \nridge begins to flatten early next week and zonal flow \nestablishes aloft again.",
